Getting ready for my ascension run, I decided to configure my
autopickup options. (for instance I normally pick up all food except
for corpses, I am bringing all the food I will need with me now, and I
dont want to do that anymore (I am a chronic packrat))

I decided that I dont want to autopickup anything except for wands of
death,scrolls of taming,potions of full healing and artifacts (and
maybe one or two others).

I found that you cant set autopickup_types to nothing, because if you
do it takes "nothing" as "everything"!

After a bit of fiddling, the only way I can achieve my means
(autopickup only the best items) is to set autopickup to something
like "=" (rings only) and throw in a 
AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTIONS:">*ring*" (never pick up any rings)
and use autopickup_exceptions for what I DO want picked up.
This is an ugly hack, to say the least, and may not be an obvious
solution to another user.

Is there a better way to do this?

Also, what do other people out there use for autopickup_exceptions on
the ascension run?
As for me, this is what I will use...

OPTIONS=autopickup,pickup_types:=
autopickup_exception=">*ring*"
autopickup_exception="<*wand of death*"
autopickup_exception="<*scroll of taming"
autopickup_exception="<*full healing*"
autopickup_exception="<*gain energy*"
autopickup_exception="<*gain level*"
autopickup_exception="<*the*"
autopickup_exception="<*The*"
autopickup_exception="<*life saving*"

